              "login": "pr-pundit-code-review"
            },
            "body": "<!-- pr-pundit-live:primus-1336-0c78dab8 -->\n### PR Pundit review\n1 finding.\n\n| # | | Finding | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 🔵 | No regression test for skipping prefetch when `data_iterator` is None | `primus/backends/megatron/patches/delayed_fp8_scaling_patches.py:269` |\n\n<details><summary>Nits and less certain findings (1)</summary>\n\n**1. No regression test for skipping prefetch when `data_iterator` is None** (`primus/backends/megatron/patches/delayed_fp8_scaling_patches.py:269`)\n\nNo test covers the new `data_iterator is not None` guard in `_patched_train_step`, so reverting the hunk leaves the suite green. Before the fix, `CudaPrefetchIterator(None)` raised `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not an iterator` on the first step. That happens on pipeline stages that get no data iterator; with TP=1 these are likely the middle stages, since Megatron normally builds data on both the first and last stage. A small test could install the patch with `tp_size=1` and mocked CUDA streams, call the wrapped train_step with `data_iterator=None`, and assert that `_prefetch_state` has no `'iter'`.\n\n**Who is affected:** Future regressions would hit Megatron runs with delayed FP8 scaling, TP=1 and pipeline parallelism, on stages that have no data iterator.\n\n_Verified by running it._\n\n</details>",
